     6	- **Language.** Clean throughout. No oath is given or implied.
     7	- **Violence.** One bout between friends under a coach's rule, with every cost carried: a forearm cut to the bruise five times, a hip, a shoulder, ten slow counts twice, and Ephram's shoulder put out and set on the oak. No blood, no gore. The injury is named by Cael as a cost he failed to price, and by Ephram as a thing he would have minded more had it been meant.
     8	- **Moral weight.** The movement prices honesty kept at a cost. Karis argues a true case to a seat that cannot be moved and leaves out the truest thing she knows. Ilsev reads into the public record the one thing her clearance allows. Withrow keeps a recommendation back for four days so that the going is his own. Brom neither signs nor refuses. Cael writes down, before the bout, that he will take something from a friend and never say so, and enters it afterward as owing. Nobody in the movement lies.
     9	- **Romance.** None.
    10	- **Audio.** Every line in the five-way council is attributed. Brom and Bracken never share a spoken list. Role names stand for the unnamed (the house's counsel, the district officer, the healer, Rooke's clerk, the Current girl, the Stone, the lake house's Blade).
