   112	## New canon minted (flag where marked)
   113	
   114	- **Call days / "keeping within the bell" (flag):** four days before a ruling; a seat or its evaluation seat may recall a party on an hour's notice; used twice in the counsel's time (once for a guild master's mother's maiden name). A return made on a call day is posted in the porch before the ruling.
   115	- **The wool-factors' guesting-house (flag):** old brick, a back gallery, in the lane behind the exchange; a parlour with a two-paned door; a flagged yard with a pump, a pentice of woolsacks and **an old screw wool press** (two posts, a beam, a wooden screw, a six-foot platen, a four-bar capstan). The woman who keeps it is unnamed.
   116	- **The district hall (flag):** three streets from the exchange; a blue door; a board of sittings beside it (the first sitting after the year's close: six names, Lira's the fourth); a second board on which the frame-house's reservations are written. The district's frame is "the size of a hay wagon"; **the plate is warm when it lights**; the assessors let the load down on springs and then again; they say only *stand there* and *thank you*.
   117	- **The district station on the north road (flag):** low stone, slate roof, a windowless frame-house behind, a sigil in the lintel, a bench, a board of hours; short of the toll-bar. **The district officer** there: stout, fair, unhurried, kind. The girl and her mother are unnamed; her Path is not given.
   118	- **The count of the room (day 187):** 187 on the benches, 19 by office, 206 with Cael. Jent has a clerk (thin, young, unnamed).
   119	- **Karis's closing (text mine, ch49)** and its count: thirty slips written, five cut in rehearsal, nine more dropped on her feet; fifty-one minutes.
   120	- **The standing entries (text mine)** and the pasted certificate form; **"evaluator of record" as the form's column heading** for the protocol's certifying office (see owner flag 2).
   121	- **Karis's supplemental (flag):** four recorded instances of a seat proceeding without the certificate — a guild hall's frame, two hill-district station frames, a plate.
   122	- **The evaluation seat's return (text mine around the protected and verbatim lines, ch50):** a designation "governs who must be present at an evaluation, and to what office its result is sent"; Ilsev's stated obligation to lay such a matter before the proceedings.
   123	- **Ilsev's appearance (flag, minor):** a spare woman of sixty or so, grey hair cut short, a plain coat.
   124	- **Havel (flag):** the copyists' loft over the long room (the factors' old sample loft; four desks; one copyist on a call day); the porch's public-record board behind a brass grille with the junior chair's key; the senior chair's bad tooth; the form *Request for relief from rotation* with five heads, and his entries.
   125	- **The ruling (text mine, ch51):** a recital and five heads; **the revocation takes effect at the close of the academic year**; the date of re-evaluation "to be notified".
   126	- **The district's notice (flag):** the code gives a district five days' notice for a compelled evaluation; the clerk reserved the frame-house for the year's last day before the ruling; the notice will be addressed to the Chancellor, to produce the enrollee.
   127	- **Seln's reading of the engrossment (flag):** registry stock from the first mould, the mark true, the die's rim number, the seat's own clerk's hand; and his four grades said aloud to Cael for the first time.
   128	- **Copy-sets (flag):** Withrow's order that the thirty-four houses that wrote and the five faculties have the ruling and the standing entries in the house's fair copy, three leaves to a set, by the next first bag.
   129	- **The district's finding (text mine)** and **the guidance note (text mine; flag):** a printed slip issued by rule with every finding; a paragraph the clerk marks where a practitioner has "associations of record"; Bracken issued it eleven times as a district clerk.
   130	- **Karis's forfeiture sheet (text mine):** eight heads; a second Greyvane request (the founders' correspondence), sealed by the fee office in the week the first was paid, answer expected in about eight weeks, redirected care of an instrument-maker at Denvash.
   131	- **Ephram (flag):** the chart's back, both lines; the three cuts chained "as a mason lays a course", and **the short cut** (heel and edge, no hip); he lays lines with a turn of the wrist and can hold two; **a Blade reads a Storm lane as a line**; "Every Blade's got a door in him. They tell you in the second year. They don't tell you where."
   132	- **Blade-adjacent as acquired (flag):** an edge "said" a hand's breadth out beyond the wood; a line past the tip along which the Blade has word of what will cross; at integration, one breath in which every edge in the yard is seen; the first pull asks *Edge?* of a lintel's arris; naming quiets it; housed beside Anchor.
   133	- **The give against an edge (flag):** the cup holds a blow and does not hold a declared edge.
   134	- **The Crown yard:** Rooke's board text (ch53); the stand's registrar's chair; **the boards custom** (the loser chalks it himself, the same day, in the other's sight; "older than the brass on the Copper crown"); the rule above the Iron column.
   135	- **Rooke's clerk** is the program's clerk who kept the visitors' ledger; the bout is entered in the program's book and the house's.
