editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:7:**Verdict: CLOSE AFTER ONE BOUNDED SAME-AUTHOR REPAIR.** The movement does what the packet asked: the year is loved before it is priced, the suite is taught with its bills, the band and the honest floor are both on the page, service lands as an event, and the procedure's findings arrive in order and end on the corridor and the pole. No scene needs rebuilding and the developed bout and the honest floor should not be shortened. What stands between it and closing is line-level: one running motif (Hesk's clock) that contradicts closed Book 5 in three places; two sentences that put the Storm notice's first reading in the wrong room; two one-clause slips (Ephram's captaincy; where Seln's "arithmetic" was said); one owner item the Tier B first page forces (the address "Cael" against the registry name *Caelen Hesk-ward*); and a residue of about thirty sentences in ch5–ch7 that keep a source sentence's content and order under the 8-word gate, concentrated in the procedure night. The procedure's beat order is the plan's and is not at issue; the sentences are.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:25:**A fluent thirteen-year-old.** The dawn run is followable because it goes one thing at a time and each thing has a bill ("Five of five"; "the shoulder spoke, low, the way it always spoke at the fourth"). "Three lies and the truth" is a teachable idea they will remember. The instrument's language is heavy ("compelled re-evaluation under standard Arbiter protocol") but the chapter translates it at once (a station, a frame, "I'm the frame"), and "corridor" is exactly the image for that reader. Withrow's morning after is concrete (a ferryman with a family and a licence). Places they may trip: the rating composite (ch2:87); "which on these boards meant five, and never the fifth" (ch3:111 — is five allowed or not?); *adduced* (ch6:73) and *in abeyance* (Tier B); "He looked at the three short steps" (ch7:65 — the code's steps, heard as stairs); the two counsels in one paragraph (ch6:21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:88:2. **The Tier B runs.** Now patterned in `protected-patterns.txt` (the first page; chapter fourteen); `source_overlap.py` reads 0 unprotected shared runs of ≥8 words. Closed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:89:3. **"upon a schedule of one academic year".** Accept. BOOK_MAP §2 mandates the change ("term-length schedule becomes the year's schedule") and Tier B permits recomposition for the calendar if the author says so, which the report does. Optional: "upon the schedule of the academic year" is a shade plainer by ear.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:126:**A. Protected, Tier B and packet lines at 1.00 — allowed, not findings.** ch5:75–83 the first page (five runs; one at 0.81 for the §2 recomposition); ch6:47 and ch7:57–61 chapter fourteen (Tier B); ch7:127 the corridor line; ch7:151–153 the stratum lines; ch7:217 Lira's question; ch7:235 the pole; ch2:63 "heavier… from the rail"; ch5:89 "nine hundred times"; ch2:125 "the first one I've ever wanted to stay in"; ch3:45 "it is a formality… Your family's ledger closes"; ch1:217 *load-bearing calm*; ch6:173 Vastin's advisory (B5 §10). Also the plan's own facts rendered as form lines: ch3:39 the docket's two lines (0.50, 0.61) — plain facts of canon (Path, tier, the year's last Fifth-day, the district seat); re-order the docket's fields if the coordinator wants the chapter at 0%, otherwise leave.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:176:| 45 | ch7:77–81 | "the file is sealed. Not destroyed. Nobody destroys a record. Sealed, so that he can't read it, and nobody he pays can read it"; "their association with him is under restriction, which in the registry's language means: decide this morning whether you would like to be next"; "this house would answer every question about him to an office that had settled the answers before it asked"; "A town can put you out of its gate… This shuts every door on the continent against you on one morning, by one post, and the paper never runs out"; "I administered two. In my registry years. The first was a man who had done worse than the registry ever knew, and I've never been sorry. The second I think about." | ch2:87 "Records — sealed, not destroyed; you can't consult them and neither can anyone acting for you"; "notified that the association is *under restriction*, which is registry language for *decide now whether you'd like to be next*"; "the academy answers questions about him to an office that has already decided the answers"; "Denvash put you out of a gate. This puts you out of every door on the continent at once, by paperwork, and the paperwork never expires"; "I administered two of them, in my registry years. One of them deserved worse. I think about the other one." | 0.36 / 0.38 / 0.41 — five sentences in the source's order with the source's phrases; the Tier B protects only "It's expulsion that follows you." The ferry pass, the guild hall and the daughter are the author's and carry the scene; re-compose the five around them |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:179:| 48 | ch7:121–125 | "I'll choose the word with care, because care is the only thing we have on this table tonight… It is not a trick. I want that minuted. A trick needs a trickster. Somebody bribed, a frame tampered with, a finding written false. There's none of that in this paper… Every clause is law, and every step is a procedure that honest officers will carry out in good faith, with clean hands. And it won't matter how honest they are. The end was fixed the morning they filed it." | ch2:107 "I want to be precise about the word, because precision is the only defense we have left tonight. Not *rigged*. Rigging requires a rigger — an assessor bought, a frame tampered with, a finding falsified — and this instrument requires none of that and contains none of it. Every clause in it is real law. Every step is a real procedure… the outcome was determined the moment the petition was filed… and every honest official who touches it… can act with total integrity and the result will not change by a hair." | 0.45; the paragraph that sets up the Tier B corridor line, nearly clause for clause. Either re-compose or the coordinator protects it as the corridor line's setup |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:181:| 50 | ch7:139–145 | "It was how her findings came when they were not findings yet."; "Every paper anybody ever filed against him went at the clause… This one doesn't even try. It leaves the clause in our hands… and asks for one thing only, which is a station. A frame. An Arbiter… The clause keeps him on a floor in front of people, where the Arbiter never comes. They don't want the clause. They want the floor." | ch2:115–117 "the way her findings sometimes came when they were not yet findings"; "The assay clause worked… because it bypasses Arbiter evaluation entirely. Evaluation by demonstration — a floor, a panel, witnesses, a record. No Arbiter in the loop… this petition's one non-negotiable demand is that he stand in front of an Arbiter. They've conceded the provision… the one thing they will not concede is the *stratum*." | 0.38; the two Tier B sentences are allowed; the argument before them tracks |
