editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:199:1. **Seln and Shadow (coordinator ruling not applied).** The task's standing ruling says Seln learns why Shadow was sealed "in Book 6 Ch15, in this movement, as the plan and Book 5's ledger reserve it", and to follow the packet for how much. Every source I can find places that telling at **source** Book 6 Ch15, *The Cache*: BOOK_MAP §3 item 15 ("Cael tells Seln the mechanism; the Shadow seal and its cost; 'You kept my file too, then.'"), §6 (Seln "does not know a sealed thing exists until M6"), §9 (the integration mechanism "Expands to Seln only (M6)"), and B5's BOOK_MAP/packets ("B6 Ch15 tells him", meaning the source chapter). Edition chapter 15 is in M3, which may be the source of the confusion. The M3 packet calls for no telling at all ("Seln's method shown; his case not mentioned aloud"), and telling him why Shadow is sealed would require telling him the integration mechanism four movements early, and would strand the Tier A line "You kept my file too, then." So **Seln is not told in M3**. If the owner does want it here, it needs a packet line, and the cache scene in M6 will need replanning.
