editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:213:1. **The eighth's log line (Tier B) — middle composed.** §8 gives *Eight. Taken from someone the system sent namelessly, to hold me namelessly… Write it down anyway.* with an ellipsis, and the packet gives "Eight… a hand and no face." Because no source chapter was opened, the words between are mine (ch32): *No paper. No seal. No office to write to, not even a false one this time. She stood in the road and did the best thing she knew how to do, and I took it off her, and she'll go home tonight to wherever they keep her and nobody will ask her how her day was. A hand and no face. I don't know what I owe someone I can't find. I don't know if owing is the word.* If the source's full text must stand, the coordinator can drop it in between the two kept fragments; nothing else in the chapter depends on my wording.
