editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/AUTHORSHIP.md:19:**No source chapter was opened.** Per the new binding method, I did not open, read, `cat`, `grep` or `--show` any file under `books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/` at any point in this session — not before drafting, not during, not after. The packet's "Read before drafting" line was not followed. The only contact with the source was mechanical and blind: `skeleton_probe.py` and `sweep_probe.sh` were run **without `--show`**, so they printed percentages per chapter and per scene and never a source sentence; and `ed.sh overlap` printed only the manuscript side of each shared run. Where a scene probed high, I re-composed it from my own event list without seeing what it matched.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-005/AUTHORSHIP.md:21:**What I read.** The compiled prompt in full (profile; formula §§2–6, 8–9; the M5 packet; the previous ending ch27 as compiled; the edition brief; BOOK_MAP §§1–13; STATE_LEDGER with AFTER M1–M4; CANON_RULES; owner voice). M4's AUTHORSHIP and AUTHOR-REPORT (for shape). The current manuscript ch27 from disk (it carried recheck line fixes since the compile: Lira's question now written in capitals; Seln's horse question), ch1 opening and suite run, ch13's Havel window, ch22's Seln window, ch24's opening (bout voice), and greps of ch1–27 for geography and recurring details. The edition's Book 5 ch56 (how a reach and a notice are rendered on this edition's page). Book 7's BOOK_MAP and STATE_LEDGER greps for Anchor's later behaviour ("wants doorways"; "can release a laid point from inside"). All of these are edition files, not source chapters.
