books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-20.md-13-Ephram's whole arc had come to this board, and Cael ran the arc on the way up, in order, the way he ran everything. A promise made two years before at the top of a stair to sixty people: *I'll wait for the semester evaluation.* A year spent being the fool who held a verdict about a session he was never allowed to watch. An empty Crown yard at the end of that year, and a man who had come to explain his own mistake to Cael's face rather than let the promise quietly lapse. A tournament, and a Gold-tier fact stopping mid-trial to read the man he had decided to stand beside, and *still glad*. And now the walls that had spent a year deciding what Cael was, about to be resigned from, and the last currency the place had ever spoken that a debt was owed in.
